    "reasoning": "Nitpicks: (1) The screenshots don\u2019t visibly show the year \"2026\" in the date chips; this is more a verification limitation than a clear error if the agent did select the right dates. (2) Currency shown in EUR (location Germany) isn\u2019t necessarily wrong for the task.\n\nCritical issues: (1) Nonstop filter not actually applied in the final evidence. The latest results screenshot (13) shows the Stops dialog with \"Any number of stops\" selected, directly contradicting the agent\u2019s claim that the nonstop filter was applied. Even if many displayed results are labeled \"Nonstop,\" failing to apply the required filter is a hard-constraint miss. (2) The agent\u2019s comparison appears inaccurate/hallucinated: it claims the three lowest visible options are all \u20ac154 (with specific evening departure times 8:45 PM and 10:00 PM), but screenshot 13 only clearly supports one \u20ac154 itinerary (IndiGo 3:00 AM\u20135:55 AM, 2h55m) and shows other visible prices like \u20ac159/\u20ac160/\u20ac161. Thus the agent did not reliably identify the three lowest visible options, nor are the reported details for two of the three options supported by the evidence.\n\nOutcome: The agent did reach a Google Flights results state for DEL\u2194BLR on the requested days (month/day) with 1 passenger and economy, and it did not book. However, because it did not (per evidence) enable nonstop-only and because the core deliverable\u2014an accurate comparison of the three lowest visible nonstop options and a recommendation based on them\u2014contains major unsupported/incorrect specifics, an average user would not be able to trust or use the recommendation. Therefore the task is not successfully completed.",
